{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>the head of the beginning, Judah, for prayer</b> — the meaning: Asaph is the head, and at the beginning of the service it is Judah, at the time of prayer first, and after that his brothers. And so בני יהודה according to the correct reading, and so Joshua 10." "<b>and Bakbukiah, second from his brothers</b> — in being second to Asaph."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Resolved יהושיע ה' as Joshua 10 by inference, though the exact verse referenced is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:37.051999637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}